* Example C01: Two-level full factorial with center points (factor table).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=FACTORIAL
  NAME1=Temp LOW1=150 HIGH1=200 NAME2=Time LOW2=10 HIGH2=30
  NAME3=Press LOW3=1 HIGH3=3 NAME4=Stir LOW4=100 HIGH4=300
  RANDOMIZE=YES SCREENINGCENTERPTS=YES SCREENINGCENTERPTSCOUNT=4
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_factorial.

* Example C02: Replicated and blocked factorial (lists).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=FACTORIAL
  VARNAMES=Temp Time Press LOWS=150 10 1 HIGHS=200 30 3 FACTORS=YES YES YES
  REPLICATES=2 BLOCKS=2 RANDOMIZE=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_blocked.

* Example C03: Fractional factorial (6 factors in 16 runs).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=FACTORIAL
  VARNAMES=A B C D E F LOWS=-1 HIGHS=1 FACTORS=YES TRIALS=16
  /OUTPUT CONFOUNDING=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_fraction.

* Example C04: Plackett-Burman screening design.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=PLACKETTBURMAN
  NAME1=Temp LOW1=150 HIGH1=200 NAME2=Time LOW2=10 HIGH2=30 NAME3=Press LOW3=1 HIGH3=3
  NAME4=Stir LOW4=100 HIGH4=300 NAME5=pH LOW5=5 HIGH5=8 NAME6=Feed LOW6=1 HIGH6=2
  NAME7=Purge LOW7=0 HIGH7=10
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_pb.

* Example C05: Definitive screening design.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=DSD
  VARNAMES=Temp Time Press Stir pH Feed LOWS=150 10 1 100 5 1 HIGHS=200 30 3 300 8 2
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_dsd.

* Example C06: Central composite design (response surface).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=CCD
  NAME1=Speed LOW1=80 HIGH1=120 NAME2=Feed LOW2=0.15 HIGH2=0.25 NAME3=Depth LOW3=1.5 HIGH3=2.5
  RANDOMIZE=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_ccd.

* Example C07: Box-Behnken design.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=BOXBEHNKEN
  VARNAMES=Dose TempC Ratio LOWS=5 40 0.5 HIGHS=15 60 1.5
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_bb.

* Example C08: General full factorial with a 3-level categorical factor.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=FULLFACTORIAL
  NAME1=Material LEVELS1=3 FACTOR1=YES NAME2=TestTemp LOW2=20 HIGH2=80 LEVELS2=2
  REPLICATES=2
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_full.

* Example C09: D-optimal design for a quadratic model.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=OPTIMAL
  VARNAMES=Temp Press Speed LOWS=100 1 10 HIGHS=200 5 50 LEVELS=3 3 3
  MODEL=QUAD TRIALS=15
  /OPTIONS CRITERION=D INITIAL=NULLIFICATION REPEATS=10
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_optimal.

* Example C10: Latin hypercube (computer experiments).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=LHS
  VARNAMES=Load Speed Gap LOWS=10 100 0.1 HIGHS=50 500 0.5 TRIALS=20 ROUNDTOS=1 0 3
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_lhs.

* Example C11: Taguchi orthogonal array.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=TAGUCHI
  VARNAMES=A B C D LOWS=1 HIGHS=2 FACTORS=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_taguchi.

* Example C12: Simplex-lattice mixture design.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=SIMPLEXLATTICE
  VARNAMES=Polymer Plasticizer Filler LATTICEDEGREE=2 AUGMENTMIX=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_lattice.

* Example C13: Simplex-centroid mixture design.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=SIMPLEXCENTROID
  VARNAMES=Polymer Plasticizer Filler
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_centroid.

* Example C14: Extreme-vertices design (constrained mixture).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=EXTREMEVERTICES
  VARNAMES=Mg NaNO3 SrNO3 Binder LOWS=0.40 0.10 0.10 0.03 HIGHS=0.60 0.50 0.50 0.08
  EVDEGREE=1
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_ev.

* Example C15: Number of factors with default names and ranges.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=FACTORIAL NFACTORS=5
  NAME2=Temp LOW2=150 HIGH2=200
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_nfactors.

* Example C16: Factor table read from the active dataset (any number of factors).
DATASET ACTIVATE factorsheet.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=PLACKETTBURMAN FACTORSFROMDATA=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_sheet.

* Example C17: Central composite design with a categorical factor.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=CCD
  NAME1=Temp LOW1=150 HIGH1=200 NAME2=Time LOW2=10 HIGH2=30
  NAME3=Supplier LEVELS3=3 FACTOR3=YES
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_ccdcat.

* Example C18: Split-plot design (hard-to-change factor).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=YES DESIGNTYPE=FULLFACTORIAL
  VARNAMES=Oven Press Mix LOWS=150 1 1 HIGHS=200 3 2 LEVELS=2 2 2
  REPLICATES=3 RANDOMIZE=YES HTC=Oven
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_split.

* Example C19: Power and sample size.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO
  /POWER POWERTABLE=YES POWEREFFECTSIZES=1 1.5 2 POWERRUNS=8 16 32 POWERALPHA=0.05 POWERTARGET=0.8.

* Example C19B: Runs needed for a target power.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO
  /POWER POWERTABLE=YES POWEREFFECTSIZES=0.5 1 1.5 2 POWERTARGET=0.9.

* Example C20: Augment a factorial to a central composite design.
DATASET ACTIVATE firstorder.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO AUGMENTTOCCD=YES AUGMENTCENTERPTS=3
  FACTORVARS=A B C RESPONSEVAR=Y
  /SAVE DATASET=plan_augmented.

* Example A01: Two-level factorial with center points: default analysis and charts.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst
  RESPONSEVAR=Yield ANALYZE=YES
  /OUTPUT PARETOPLOT=YES MAINEFFECTS=YES INTERACTIONS=YES CUBEPLOT=YES RESIDUALPLOTS=YES
  /FITMODEL EFFECTSPLOT=YES.

* Example A02: Own model per response and predictions.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst
  RESPONSEVAR=Yield Cost ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL TERMS="Yield: Temp Time Press Catalyst Temp*Time CTPT; Cost: Temp Time Press Temp*Press"
    PREDICT="Temp=190 Time=25 Press=1 Catalyst=B; Temp=160 Time=12 Press=3 Catalyst=A".

* Example A03: Automatic term selection (stepwise).
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst
  RESPONSEVAR=Cost ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL SELECTION=STEPWISE ALPHAENTER=0.15 ALPHAREMOVE=0.10.

* Example A04: Box-Cox transformation.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst
  RESPONSEVAR=Visc ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL BOXCOX=AUTO TERMSET=ts_linear.

* Example A05: Fractional factorial screening: aliasing and Lenth's method.
DATASET ACTIVATE screen5.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=A B C D E RESPONSEVAR=Response ANALYZE=YES
  /OUTPUT PARETOPLOT=YES
  /FITMODEL EFFECTSPLOT=YES.

* Example A06: Plackett-Burman screening analysis.
DATASET ACTIVATE pb11.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO DESIGNTYPE=PLACKETTBURMAN
  FACTORVARS=F1 F2 F3 F4 F5 F6 F7 F8 F9 F10 F11 RESPONSEVAR=Response ANALYZE=YES
  /OUTPUT PARETOPLOT=YES.

* Example A07: Response surface (CCD): quadratic model, canonical analysis, contours.
DATASET ACTIVATE machining.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Speed Feed Depth RESPONSEVAR=Rough ANALYZE=YES
  /OUTPUT CONTOURPLOT=YES
  /FITMODEL CANONICAL=YES SURFACEPLOT=YES.

* Example A08: Box-Behnken analysis.
DATASET ACTIVATE purify.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO DESIGNTYPE=BOXBEHNKEN FACTORVARS=Dose TempC Ratio
  RESPONSEVAR=Purity ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL CANONICAL=YES.

* Example A09: General factorial with a categorical factor and Tukey grouping.
DATASET ACTIVATE materials.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Material TestTemp RESPONSEVAR=Strength ANALYZE=YES
  /OUTPUT MAINEFFECTS=YES INTERACTIONS=YES
  /FITMODEL GROUPING=YES.

* Example A10: Two 3-level text factors, numeric factor as categorical.
DATASET ACTIVATE suppliers.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Supplier Machine Temp RESPONSEVAR=Thickness ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL CATEGORICAL=Temp GROUPING=YES.

* Example A11: Blocked factorial with center points.
DATASET ACTIVATE shifts.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=A B C RESPONSEVAR=Strength ANALYZE=YES.

* Example A12: Factors not named: detected from the data.
DATASET ACTIVATE machining.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO RESPONSEVAR=Life ANALYZE=YES.

* Example A13: Mixture analysis (Scheffe model) with trace plot.
DATASET ACTIVATE blend.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Polymer Plasticizer Filler RESPONSEVAR=Elongation ANALYZE=YES
  OPTIMIZERESPONSE=YES OPTIMIZATIONGOAL=MAXIMIZE
  /FITMODEL MIXMODEL=QUADRATIC TRACEPLOT=YES.

* Example A14: Taguchi signal-to-noise analysis.
DATASET ACTIVATE taguchi.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO DESIGNTYPE=TAGUCHI FACTORVARS=A B C D
  RESPONSEVAR=Y1 Y2 Y3 ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL SNTYPE=LARGER.

* Example A15: Split-plot analysis (REML).
DATASET ACTIVATE ovens.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Oven Press Mix RESPONSEVAR=Y ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL TERMS="Oven Press Mix Oven*Press Oven*Mix Press*Mix".

* Example A16: Analyze variability (dispersion effects).
DATASET ACTIVATE spread.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=A B RESPONSEVAR=Y ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL VARIABILITY=YES.

* Example A17: Uncertainty map.
DATASET ACTIVATE machining.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Speed Feed Depth RESPONSEVAR=Rough ANALYZE=YES
  /OUTPUT UNCERTAINTYMAP=YES.

* Example A18: Legacy raw-unit analysis with variable selection.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press RESPONSEVAR=Yield ANALYZE=YES
  VARSELECT=YES VARSELMETHOD=STEPWISE STEPDIR=BOTH SELECTIONTRACE=YES
  /FITMODEL ANALYSISMODEL=LEGACY
  /OUTPUT EFFECTSTABLE=YES RESIDUALTESTS=YES VIFTABLE=YES.

* Example O01: Single response: minimize surface roughness.
DATASET ACTIVATE machining.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Speed Feed Depth RESPONSEVAR=Rough ANALYZE=YES
  OPTIMIZERESPONSE=YES OPTIMIZATIONGOAL=MINIMIZE.

* Example O02: Several responses: desirability with limits, weights, importance.
DATASET ACTIVATE machining.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Speed Feed Depth RESPONSEVAR=Rough Life ANALYZE=YES
  OPTIMIZERESPONSE=YES OPTIMIZATIONGOALS=MINIMIZE MAXIMIZE
  /OPTIMIZE LOWERS=0 40 UPPERS=4 0 WEIGHTS=1 2 IMPORTANCE=1 3 SOLUTIONS=3
    CONFIRMRUNS=3 ROBUST=YES ROBUSTSD=5 OVERLAY=YES.

* Example O03: Target value and held factor.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst RESPONSEVAR=Yield Cost ANALYZE=YES
  OPTIMIZERESPONSE=YES OPTIMIZATIONGOALS=TARGET MINIMIZE OPTIMIZATIONTARGETS=64 16
  /OPTIMIZE LOWERS=60 0 UPPERS=68 22 HOLD="Catalyst=B".

* Example O04: Profit goal with a requirement.
DATASET ACTIVATE machining.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Speed Feed Depth RESPONSEVAR=Rough Life ANALYZE=YES
  /OPTIMIZE PROFIT='2*Life - 10*Rough - 0.05*Speed' PROFITGOAL=MAXIMIZE PROFITLIMITS="Rough<=3.5".

* Example O05: Cost goal with a categorical factor in the formula.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst RESPONSEVAR=Yield Cost ANALYZE=YES
  /FITMODEL CENTERTERM=NO
  /OPTIMIZE PROFIT='Cost + 0.01*Temp + ifelse(Catalyst=="B", 0.5, 0)' PROFITGOAL=MINIMIZE
    PROFITLIMITS="Yield>=62".

* Example N01: Next steps: path of steepest ascent.
DATASET ACTIVATE pilot.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Speed RESPONSEVAR=Conversion ANALYZE=YES.

* Example N02: Next steps after a screening experiment with curvature.
DATASET ACTIVATE reactor.
STATS DOE ANALYSIS GENERATEDESIGN=NO FACTORVARS=Temp Time Press Catalyst RESPONSEVAR=Yield Cost ANALYZE=YES
  OPTIMIZERESPONSE=YES OPTIMIZATIONGOALS=MAXIMIZE MINIMIZE.

